WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.430
- [Narrator] Ugh, brain freeze.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.770
It's awful, that sharp,
searing pain in your forehead.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.640
But you know what's even worse?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.840
Not everyone gets it.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.380
That's right, some people can suck down

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.340
as many milkshakes as they
want and never feel a thing.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.430
Life is so unfair.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.140
And you know what else?

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.313
These lucky people are
ruining it for scientists too.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.460
Brain freeze is one of
those scientific mysteries

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.160
that's been around since the 1800s.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.700
Just throw it in there
with UFOs and crop circles.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.240
We may never know the
real reason behind them.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.620
Ah, maybe that's a bit of an exaggeration

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.300
but here's the thing,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.140
the leading theories for
what causes a brain freeze

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.120
have to do with a physical response

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.173
that everyone should feel.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:57.600
The way scientists think it works is this:

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.700
Brain freeze happens when something cold

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.380
hits the roof of your mouth

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.330
where it triggers your trigeminal nerve.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.920
It's the nerve in charge
of the sensations you feel

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.010
around the front of your head.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.750
That's why when you freeze
it to sub-zero temperatures,

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.910
the pain is around the
temple and the forehead.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.460
In fact, different nerves

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.890
cause pain in different
parts of your head.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.380
A toothache, for example, can
irritate the mandibular nerve

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.793
causing pain near the central skull.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.430
But, when it comes to brain
freeze, the source of the pain

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.230
is different from most other headaches.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:36.040
Turns out it's similar to
why your feet and hands sting

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.990
when they get too cold.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.040
Your body floods that area with blood

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.060
to try and return it to body temperature

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.780
and in the process your
blood vessels expand,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.500
which causes that throbbing pain.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.760
Similarly, during a brain freeze,

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.130
blood vessels in your brain widen

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.130
sending a rush of blood
to the roof of your mouth

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.440
and, in the process, causing pain.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.890
Now, the trigeminal nerve is
a natural part of the body,

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.800
so if it's the real cause of brain freeze

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.930
then that means everyone should get it.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.250
So why do scientists estimate

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:16.990
that only 37% of Americans,
actually, feel it.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.730
And, for that matter,
41% of children in Taiwan

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:24.480
and 15% of the adults in Denmark,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.340
according to another study.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.780
Researchers can only speculate.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.550
Maybe the trigeminal
nerve is less sensitive

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.870
in certain demographics.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.760
One thing that does seem to be clear

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.330
is that people who do
experience brain freeze

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.150
may also be more susceptible

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.143
to another kind of mysterious
headache, migraines.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:48.560
In one small study, 93%
of migraine patients

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.330
were also prone to brain freeze,

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.160
which has led researchers to suspect

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.550
that the trigeminal nerve

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.650
also plays a key role in migraines.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.963
Whatever the reason, just hang in there.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.350
Brain freezes, usually,
only last 20 or 30 seconds.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.410
You could take those seconds

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.823
to remember not to slurp
so quickly next time.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.090
What else do you want to
know about the human body?

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.690
Let us know in the comments
and thanks for watching.

